Source: libdtfl
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 autoconf,
 automake,
 libtool,
 pkg-config
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Section: libs
Homepage: https://codeberg.org/gregburd/libdtfl
Vcs-Git: https://codeberg.org/gregburd/libdtfl.git
Vcs-Browser: https://codeberg.org/gregburd/libdtfl
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libdtfl0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: timely and differential dataflow for C (shared library)
 libdtfl is a C11 port of timely dataflow, differential dataflow, and
 the timely diagnostics tools: a data-parallel runtime for cyclic
 dataflows with progress tracking, incrementally maintained collections
 with join, reduce, iterate and shared arrangements, graph algorithms
 and worst-case-optimal joins, and an in-process diagnostics server.
 .
 This package contains the shared library.

Package: libdtfl-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends: libdtfl0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: timely and differential dataflow for C (development files)
 libdtfl is a C11 port of timely dataflow, differential dataflow, and
 the timely diagnostics tools: a data-parallel runtime for cyclic
 dataflows with progress tracking, incrementally maintained collections
 with join, reduce, iterate and shared arrangements, graph algorithms
 and worst-case-optimal joins, and an in-process diagnostics server.
 .
 This package contains the static library, the public headers, the
 pkg-config metadata, and the manual pages needed to build against
 libdtfl.

Package: libdtfl-tools
Architecture: any
Depends: libdtfl0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: timely and differential dataflow for C (command-line tools)
 libdtfl is a C11 port of timely dataflow, differential dataflow, and
 the timely diagnostics tools.
 .
 This package contains the dtfl-diag diagnostics client, the dtfl-ddir
 dataflow compiler, and the dtfl-server plugin host, with their manual
 pages.
